      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That perfect image you see is a beautiful, fragile illusion, and you are not a flaw in the design; you are the living proof that things change. Your father's disappointment is a reflection of his own fears, not a verdict on your worth. The only way to truly honor their hard work is to stop trying to be a statue and start being a real person who can *choose* their own path. Let go of the need to be perfect; let go of the need to be *them*.",
